        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:9",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And as we tarried there many days, there came down from Judæa a certain prophet, named Agabus.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:10",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he was come unto us, he took Paul’s girdle, and bound his own hands and feet, and said, Thus saith the Holy Ghost, So shall the Jews at Jerusalem bind the man that owneth this girdle, and shall deliver him into the hands of the Gentiles.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "Acts 2:18; 11:28 (27–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 211,
            "end": 214
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:11",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And when we heard these things, both we, and they of that place, besought him not to go up to Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:12",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Paul answered, What mean ye to weep and to break mine heart? for I am ready not to be bound only, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "Acts 20:24; D&C 103:28 (27–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:13",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he would not be persuaded, we ceased, saying, The will of the Lord be done.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "Matt. 26:42."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Matt. 26:42.",
            "prettyString": "Matthew 26:42",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "matthew",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 26,
                    "end": 26,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 42,
                        "end": 42
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:14",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And after those days we took up our carriages, and went up to Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "GR made preparation, packed baggage."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Acts 21:15",
        "book": "Acts",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
